---
# Static analysis for the shipped code (src/), run nightly by
# static-analysis.yml and by hand with the linux-gcc-tidy preset
# (docs/static-analysis.md). The compiler warning set it complements is in
# cmake/CompilerWarnings.cmake; those warnings are errors in every build, these
# are the checks that need a whole program.
#
# The families are the ones that find defects: the Clang Static Analyzer, bug,
# cert, concurrency, performance and portability. Style is not here - it is
# .clang-format's and the compiler's - and the tests are not tidied: Catch2's
# REQUIRE/CHECK macros expand to code these checks cannot see through
# (tests/CMakeLists.txt clears the launcher). The checks switched off below are
# off for a reason, not for a count:
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#       Two adjacent parameters of the same type are everywhere in a protocol
#       codec (address and port, offset and length); the names are the check's
#       only defence and they are already the defence.
#   bugprone-exception-escape
#       Every interface method is noexcept by contract, including the ones
#       that allocate: an allocation failure terminates the operation rather
#       than unwinding through it. The check cannot see that contract.
#   bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion
#       A block pool keeps its free-list link in the block itself, so memcpy
#       takes the address of a std::byte*; the conversion is the pool's
#       representation, and the check reports it through every translation unit
#       that includes the interface.
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise
#       Shifts and masks in the wire, CRC and hash code mix unsigned values with
#       the int literals of their shift counts; the signedness that matters is
#       caught by -Wsign-conversion.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange
#       The check assumes an enumerator's list is all the values the type can
#       hold. StatusCode has a fixed std::uint16_t underlying type and ARINC
#       615A-3 6.4.10 carries any 16-bit code in an ABORT message.
#   performance-enum-size
#       The wire enums name their underlying type for the field they are
#       written into, not for the smallest type that holds today's enumerators.
#   performance-no-int-to-ptr
#       A memory region's address is a pointer-sized integer until the pool
#       hands the storage out; that cast is the pool's interface.
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once
#       #pragma once is the project's include guard; the check prefers named
#       guards, which this tree does not use.
Checks: >
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  concurrency-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/.*'
# A toolchain's own headers (the MSVC STL under a local Windows run) are not
# this project's code, and a local build does not mark them as system headers.
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: 'Program Files'
FormatStyle: file

CheckOptions:
  # Ignoring an error that the interface reports is sometimes the contract:
  # a cleanup after a failure cannot do better than try, and a best-effort send
  # is one. The code casts those to void to say so.
  bugprone-unused-return-value.AllowCastToVoid: true
